<div class="note">
  <p class="note__label">Status</p>
  <p>The Kenya-China Tea Summit is developing a programme led by practical knowledge, market evidence and real experience. Confirmed speakers will be published here once invitations are accepted and session details are approved.</p>
</div>

<h2>Areas of interest</h2>

<ol class="clauses">
  <li class="clause"><div>
    <h3>Trade and market access</h3>
    <p>Buyer requirements, routes to market, standards, certification, distribution, direct sales and commercial partnerships.</p>
  </div></li>
  <li class="clause"><div>
    <h3>Investment and finance</h3>
    <p>Processing, packaging, logistics, product development, joint ventures, insurance, agricultural finance and investment readiness.</p>
  </div></li>
  <li class="clause"><div>
    <h3>Technology and innovation</h3>
    <p>Processing equipment, field technology, traceability, quality systems, energy efficiency, agronomy and climate resilience.</p>
  </div></li>
  <li class="clause"><div>
    <h3>Products, brands and consumers</h3>
    <p>Specialty tea, green and orthodox tea, product development, packaging, branding, retail and changing consumer preferences.</p>
  </div></li>
  <li class="clause"><div>
    <h3>Tea culture and hospitality</h3>
    <p>Kenyan and Chinese tea traditions, preparation, service, tourism and cultural exchange.</p>
  </div></li>
</ol>

<h2>What makes a strong proposal</h2>

<p>We are looking for sessions with a clear purpose and a defined audience. A strong proposal should include:</p>

<ul>
  <li>A specific topic, question, case study or finding</li>
  <li>Evidence or direct experience</li>
  <li>A clear connection to the summit's Kenya-China focus</li>
  <li>Practical value for people in the room</li>
  <li>An honest description of any commercial interest</li>
</ul>

<p>Company presentations and product pitches are better suited to the <a href="/exhibition/">exhibition</a> and <a href="/sponsorship/">partnership</a> programme.</p>

<h2>Propose a session</h2>

<p>There is no dedicated speaker form yet. Use the <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and state "Speaker proposal" in your message, together with your organisation, proposed topic and which area of interest above it fits.</p>

<p>Submission does not guarantee a place on the programme. The summit team will confirm the review process, deadlines and speaker terms when the programme committee is in place.</p>

